Delete an archived session's sandbox, and its home volume, and keep the
conversation.

A stopped agent-sandbox keeps its Sandbox and home volume until the session
is deleted, and local-path doesn't cap that volume, so archived sessions kept
filling the node's disk until the kubelet evicted the server, Postgres and
Vault. The archive teardown, which runs once the Undo window has passed, now
also deletes the session's managed sandbox
(_delete_archived_session_sandbox), the same way deleting the session does.
It leaves the host row alone, so an unarchived session reads as asleep: its
next message tries to wake the sandbox, finds it gone, and starts a fresh one
with upstream's "workspace reset" notice and the session's repository cloned
again. Only providers that keep a stopped sandbox are touched, and a host
another unarchived session is bound to is skipped. On every start, the server
also does this for sessions that are already archived
(delete_archived_session_sandboxes), which covers sessions archived before
this patch.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0025-push-to-talk.patch.
